    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0050" n="38" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg38"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/4–3046: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Certain Diplomatic and Consular
                            Officers</hi><anchor n="36" xml:id="d41-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-30T11:00:00-04:00">April 30, 1946—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>French in Hanoi fear Chinese attack on French civilians, soldiers, any incident
                    likely become serious citywide fight. Some French believe Chinese planning
                    overrun French, overthrow Vietnam Government, establish Chinese fostered Dong
                    Minh Hoi Party in power then ask Chinese assistance thus allowing Chinese troops
                    remain Indochina. Consul Saigon suggests<anchor n="37" xml:id="d41-f2"/> general
                    order from Chiang Kai-shek might avert incident.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d41-f1" n="36" type="source" xml:id="d41-f1-content">
                <p>At Bangkok, Batavia, London, Moscow, Paris, and Singapore.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d41-f2" n="37" xml:id="d41-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 121, April 27, 1946, 10 a.m., not printed.</p>
            </note>
